  m_text: "Forests are the Florida panther\u2019s home. They give panthers places
    to hunt for food, hide, and raise their kittens safely. Deer, hogs, and other
    animals that panthers eat also live in the forest, so panthers depend on these
    places for their meals. Panthers need big, connected forests so they can move
    around without getting trapped or crossing busy roads. Protecting Florida\u2019s
    forests helps keep the panther safe and gives it the space and food it needs
    to survive."
